{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/909653-remembering-your-guilty-pleasures-of-the-90s","id":909653,"title":"Remembering your guilty pleasures of the 90s","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T18:03:02-07:00","id":909653,"title":"Remembering your guilty pleasures of the 90s","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Toned WAY down from the final version I played back in the late 90s, this is Jason Shadow-Walker, the magic-using weretiger, complete with katanas, long hair, sleeveless trenchcoat, arm-bands, fingerless gloves and so on. In this form, he's a weretiger with magic.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img924/7725/WpLCky.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Originally a character I played in a friend's White Wolf Classic World of Darkness Mage: The Ascension 1st Edition game starting in 1994, Jason Shadow-Walker was a fantastic twink-munchkin who in the end was:<br /> \u2022 A Mage (who in the end had nearly maxed out his spheres and had a very high Arete rating)<br /> \u2022 A wereitger (with many Gifts of many levels... this was before we even had 2nd Edition W:tA to work from.)<br /> \u2022 An assortment of over-powered energy weapons<br /> \u2022 A cyber-jack in his neck<br /> \u2022 A fetish laptop that had the spirit of his girlfriend inside of it<br /> \u2022 A power armor suit that was dedicated to him (eventually.)<br /> \u2022 A space ship that he used to fly around another glaxy<br /> \u2022 Was the king of a nation in a realm of D&amp;D<br /> \u2022 The trapped spirit of the weretiger in his mind that fought for control of the body from time to time.<br /> ... and a lot more that was just plain ridiculous.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I played him for many years, and I know that he's entirely not Kosher according to canon rules/setting (he started as a Mage, but due to a severe botch from another Correspondence roll with a weretiger, the two merged into one body and the two minds fought for control and the Mage won and assumed the weretiger's mind had been lost, but discovered many years later that it had only been forced deep into his mind and eventually returned and thus how he was able to retain his Avatar and weretiger powers *laugh*), and he was over-powered and a bit silly, but you know, sometimes it's just fun to play something over-the-top without a ceiling and see how far the game can go while folks still have fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> What are your favorite guilty pleasure characters that broke the &quot;rules&quot;, but were fun to play nonetheless?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:08:08-07:00","id":915613,"title":"","content":"Ddddduuuuudddddeeeeee!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! Magic using weretigers are awersome!<br /> <br /> Has to be a Khan with many gifts and Rites. And watched too much tv.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:50:30-07:00","id":915634,"title":"","content":"I once played a Kinain Dhampir Fomori Sorcerer just because I could get away with it. It was a terrible idea on multiple levels but I regret nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T12:56:56-07:00","id":918203,"title":"","content":"The first Werewolf game I ever ran had a villain who was a Black Spiral Dancer by the name of Chaos Doom-Speak, and he wore full plate armor in a modern day set game.<br /> I thought we was the radist villain that had ever villained, so much so that the only character who could truly defeat him was an NPC mage I created and thought was the bees-knees of NPC's.<br /> So the story ended with me fighting myself as the players sat back and watched...<br /> I've gotten better, I swear!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:28:03-07:00","id":918634,"title":"","content":"Dude... dual wielding katana and magic weretiger with sleeveless black trenchcoat and fingerless gloves? My pleasures weren't so guilty at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I didn't usually care for excess of rules and combos and such (that alone was heresy at the time. Storyteller without op chars? Impossibiru), so i don't have game-breaking examples, but I do have two somewhat meta examples.<br /> <br /> I loved gming werewolf games. But in my own WtA setting I liked to focus more on the personal drama of being a half-spirit creature than all the violence and metaplot. In the end my games were more akin to WtF 2e than the typical 90s WtA (just imagine my surprise and joy when WtF came out).<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Why is that guilty&quot;</i> you ask. Understand that the 90s around here in Brazil were the time of ST vs Everything Else, &quot;storyteller is the only rpg with roleplay, everything else sucks&quot;, &quot;rpg is for nerds, st is for cool people&quot;, the time of the dark and trendy teenagers playing, and that the idea of &quot;there's no wrong as long as you guys are having fun&quot; was non-existent, specially on Storyteller-based circles.<br /> <br /> So with with all the metaplot-crazy guys and powergamers, my idea of a local, personal werewolf not exactly following all the elements in the book or caring for the metaplot, but instead focusing more on the savage, personal drama was considered <i>heretical</i>. People used to get pretty heated up denoucing my games, to my amazement. Nowadays I see it as &quot;they were wrong, I was right&quot;, but it's absurd to remember that at the time I regarded it as a guilty pleasure. &quot;Haha, I don't care what they say, and I'll keep doing it and they'll keep getting angrier and angrier. I'm such an artsy rebel against those brutes!&quot;. Absurd <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Another, I loved the Bastet, even tattooed the sigil on my right arm, and my games always had a strong changing breed presence as &quot;the other guys doing their things&quot;. There was a npc, Lucy, a feline ceilican slightly based on the wackoo characters that Cameron Dias used to portray (including short blonde hair and wide smile), that as an informant served as a foil and balance to one violent group of players. The guilty pleasure was being able to act as the generic insuferable ragabash-like Bastet while the garou growled and had to put up with her. She helped a lot, and they knew she meant no harm to them and even regarded her a friend, so the bastet was the <i>&quot;crazy friend we have to put up with even if we would really really rather not, but do anyway because he's loyal or someone's brother or something like that&quot;</i> concept. Such guilty pleasure.<br /> <br /> Other breed npcs weren't as guilty and such not nearly as fulfilling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","user":"DiBastet","date":". 06-21-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:34:37-07:00","id":923054,"title":"","content":"All of my American Fenrir NPC's were based on Matthew McConaughey's character from &quot;Reign of Fire.&quot; All of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T18:54:31-07:00","id":923624,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed playing on the White Wolf website. There was it's share of crazy stuff. It had it's trolls that were more interested in ruining someone else's day than actually playing in any game. <br /> <br /> \u200bBut there were also a lot of good people who were great to be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T05:07:51-07:00","id":923793,"title":"","content":"The awesomeness of werewolf still eluded me, most of the 90s. My guilty pleasure is therefore a vampire. In the late 90s, everything was &quot;Millennium&quot; and a new vampire LARP chronicle bearing that name (admittedly for the lack of creativity on the STs part) was about to start. The ST stated before the chronicle started, that he was awarding bonus points at character creation for long and extensive backgrounds. I had just finished high school and had spare time until alternative civilian service would start. So, I took the timeline of Microsoft Encarta and started a character backstory right there, with the first recorded human history.<br /> The character went on to basically become a demi-godlike being, reaching Golconda, before being trapped and experimented on by the still new Tremere (Goratrix, precisely), who wanted that kind of power. Having lost Golconda and his blood changed with most of his disciplines gone (to meet the actual start character stats) the character was the weakest being from before the Flood. The ST liked the story, but didn't want such a character in the chronicle....<br /> <br /> However, just for fun I once created the stats for that character's Sire. I came up with 101 points in Disciplines (including Paths). Then, whenever I found a chronicle with a ST that could be easily impressed I told him about the unkillable character I had and some even let me play this being of sheer awesomeness.<br /> Or at least the projected self of the character, who used combinations of spirit thau, obfuscate, movement of the mind and chimistry to appear as if he was on the scene, while his real body actually was earth melted somewhere else on the globe.<br /> <br /> Well, that was the early 2000er years. All weird stuff. Glad I found werewolf LARP and a more serious style of play...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T08:47:09-07:00","id":923877,"title":"","content":"OK, my guilty pleasure is a Cyberpunk character named Aristotle Giovanni, loosely based on a Hunters Hunted character concept I had for a VTM game that never ran. Aristotle was a tall pale street tough in a black trenchcoat wearing sunglasses at night. He had a hot pink uzi named &quot;\u00dczzi&quot; and I swear this was all before anyone had heard of <i>The Matrix</i>. I remember one session in which a friend and I were babbling endlessly about Marcus Cole and the White Star Fleet from <i>Babylon 5</i>. Both our characters botched initiative that combat, so we concluded that our characters were the ones talking about the show in the middle of a firefight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:09:17-07:00","id":929705,"title":"","content":"*sigh* I wish I could've gamed in the 90's! Sadly, I was born in 1993 and started gaming in 2007 and didn't get into WoD until 2010.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T11:21:23-07:00","id":929847,"title":"","content":"My guilty pleasure was a mage trapped inside an gargoyle, he was the smartest most badass gargoyle ever in a vampire coterie.<br /> The name was David, Goliath the mind of the actual gargoyle was in his former Body.<br /> <br /> In modern times the mage to go was Vhorador, a Hollow One vamp Wannabee. Sleepless, immune to pain and reasoninga and enough rotes to pass as a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}